    },
    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: "Arba'a Turub",
            subtitle: 'The Somali Titan',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Arba'a Turub (literally Four Packs of Cards) is a massive-scale Somali partnership game that pushes the boundaries of traditional trick-taking. Using a staggering 144-card deck and hands of 36 cards each, it combines the structural logic of Whist with an unusual 'Progressive Win' condition that requires a team to outdo their own previous performance to claim the match.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "A unique Somali evolution of European Whist, likely developed during periods of colonial influence and adapted to local social settings. Its name 'Arba'a Turub' signifies the four decks required to play.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4 players in two fixed partnerships (North-South vs East-West).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '144 cards. Prepared by taking four 52-card decks and removing all 2s, 3s, 4s, and 5s. Ranks: A(high), K, Q, J, 10, 9, 8, 7, 6(low).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Four identical decks, table space large enough for 144 cards.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Deal starts clockwise. Each player receives 36 cards in batches of 3. **Crucial**: After the first 3 cards are dealt to the player on the dealer's left (Eldest Hand), they must declare trumps immediately.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Two-Pack Variant: A faster version using only 72 cards (two decks).',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
